  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "G Data refers to it as Uroburos, in correspondence with a string found in the malware's code and following an ancient symbol depicting a serpent or dragon eating its own tail.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s3"
      },
      "text": "Uroburos is a rootkit, composed of two files, a driver and an encrypted virtual file system.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "The development team behind this malware obviously comprises highly skilled computer experts, as you can infer from the structure and the advanced design of the rootkit.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s9"
      },
      "text": "Due to the complexity of this malware and the supposed spying techniques used by it, we assume that this rootkit targets governments, research institutes, or/and big companies.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s10"
      },
      "text": "suspected Due to many technical details (file name, encryption keys, behavior and more details mentioned in this report), we assume that the group behind Uroburos is the same group that performed a cyberattack against the United States of America in 2008 with a malware called Agent.BTZ.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s14"
      },
      "text": "According to all indications we gathered from the malware analyses and the research, we are sure of the fact that attacks carried out with Uroburos are not targeting John Doe but high profile enterprises, nation states, intelligence agencies and similar targets.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_25",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s3"
      },
      "text": "We identified several file names for the driver, for example: Ultra3.sys, msw32.sys, vstor32.sys.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_32",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 7,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p7_s2"
      },
      "text": "Virtual file systems The Uroburos rootkit uses two virtual file systems – one NTFS file system and one FAT file system.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_57",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 11,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p11_s3"
      },
      "text": "Victims and attribution Due to the complexity of the Uroburos rootkit, we estimate that it was designed to target government institutions, research institutions or companies dealing with sensitive information as well as similar high-profile targets.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_58",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 11,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p11_s4"
      },
      "text": "Concerning the attribution, we found some technical information which allows us to link the Uroburos rootkit to a cyber-attack against the United States of America, carried out in 2008 4 and, particularly, to the worm used by the attackers, called Agent.BTZ.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_60",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 11,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p11_s6"
      },
      "text": " the usage of the same obfuscation key in Uroburos and Agent.BTZ (1dM3uu4j7Fw4sjnbcwlDqet4m5Imnxl1pzxI6as80cbLnmz54cs5Ldn4ri3do5L6gs923HL34x2f 5cvd0fk6c1a0s)  the usage of the same file name to store logs: winview.ocx  Uroburos actually checks whether Agent.BTZ is already present on the attacked system, before its installation.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_62",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 11,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p11_s8"
      },
      "text": "In case someone from the audience of this report notices an infection caused by the Uroburos rootkit and needs help, would like to receive further technical information or would like to contribute any information about this case, please feel free to contact us by email using the following mailbox: intelligence@gdata.de",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_67",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "GData_Uroburos_RedPaper_EN_v1",
      "locator": {
        "page": 12,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p12_s5"
      },
      "text": "There are some strong indications which suggest that the group behind Uroburos is the same as the one behind Agent.BTZ, which allegedly was part of an intelligence agency cyberattack targeting US military bases in 2008.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
